&nbsp;


&nbsp;


Hi Everyone—

&nbsp;

Our memorandum detailing the four damages approaches is in progress and will be circulated to this group by next Monday.

&nbsp;

Attached are two documents that outline our approach to calculating damages for the IPQs:&nbsp;

Memo - Damages Calculation for IPQs.docx – This memorandum outlines our current thinking on how to calculate damages for
 the IPQs.Calculations for IPQs.xlsx – This document contains preliminary damages calculations for each claimant (see sheet “IPQs”).&nbsp;
 We have added a drop-down menu (sheet “IPQs”, cell B5) that allows you to toggle between different estimates of the percentage difference between price paid and actual value.

&nbsp;

Both documents involve approaches that are based on the marginal willingness to pay literature and VW Dieselgate event study literature.&nbsp; We may be able to add calculations based on the “illegality” and “cost
 of cure” approaches, pending further discussions and the availability of required inputs.&nbsp; We will not, however, be able to conduct our own event study in advance of the December 17 deadline.&nbsp; Please note that we are still waiting for the finalized version
 of the quantum sample claimant data, so the figures reflected in these documents are subject to change.

&nbsp;

Please let me know if you have any questions or if you would like to schedule a call to discuss.

&nbsp;

Thanks,

Neilson

