 and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thank you, Alicia. Happy to be support on this.&nbsp;@Priscilla Mendes&nbsp;- would you mind sharing the skeleton arguments for both claimant and defendant side? We need to prepare some robust background messaging and reactive statements to deal with likely press interest in a few hours' time, and I don’t believe this was captured in the recent memo you circulated.&nbsp;Thanks,Kit&nbsp;&nbsp;Kit DunfordFTI Consulting+44(0)7717 417 038From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Monday, October 6, 2025 9:42:10 AMTo: Priscilla Mendes &lt;pmendes@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dunford, Kit &lt;Kit.Dunford@fticonsulting.com&gt;; Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Dougie Inglis &lt;dInglis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Strat Comm Pogust Goodhead &lt;pogustgoodhead@fticonsulting.com&gt;Subject: [EXTERNAL] RE: Comms prep - NOx PTR &nbsp;Thanks Pri. This is helpful. We need a way to ensure that we’re splitting our priorities given the issues in BR and now emissions in the UK. Can I therefore ask that you involve @Dunford, Kit on all matters of emissions whilst you and your team focus on the BHP side. I’ll be in court with Anna. @Dunford, Kit pls can we have some messaging for the press that we’re confident in releasing. Many thanksA&nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Priscilla Mendes &lt;pmendes@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 05 October 2025 21:56To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dunford, Kit &lt;Kit.Dunford@fticonsulting.com&gt;; Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Dougie Inglis &lt;dInglis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Strat Comm Pogust Goodhead &lt;pogustgoodhead@fticonsulting.com&gt;Subject: Re: Comms prep - NOx PTR&nbsp;Hi Alicia,&nbsp;Please find attached the memo, which was prepared before the recent leadership changes in the case. It is intended for sharing with journalists interested in the claim – we have this kind of memo for all LATAM cases, as a set of pre-approved wording in place is important to streamline press requests and avoid reverting to Legal each time a new enquiry arises.&nbsp;In preparation for tomorrow’s PTR, my team has also reviewed the Defendant’s skeleton and compiled a note highlighting all mentions of PG that could present PR issues or risks – also attached.&nbsp;If Kit/FTI or Pallas have visibility on the strategy behind PG’s application to step down, it would be very helpful have their views - as my team and I have not been involved in these discussions to date&nbsp;Lastly, we received a request this afternoon from Alistair Gray, from FT, asking for a copy of PG’s skeleton for the PTR. As I understand it will only be on public domain once the hearing starts tomorrow, I have not yet responded.&nbsp;Best,&nbsp;Priscilla Mendes (she/her)​​​​ (shChief External Affairs and Strategy Officer+ 44 0 7493 014 571m Men&nbsp;From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Sunday, 5 October 2025 at 20:06To: Priscilla Mendes &lt;pmendes@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Dunford, Kit &lt;Kit.Dunford@fticonsulting.com&gt;, Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Dougie Inglis &lt;dInglis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Strat Comm Pogust Goodhead &lt;pogustgoodhead@fticonsulting.com&gt;Subject: Re: Comms prep - NOx PTRHi Pri,&nbsp;&nbsp;Do you have a copy of the memo you mentioned to circulate to this group? I assume there will be a lot of legal press from the application being heard tomorrow. I’d like us to be able to fend off the provocative headlines as the very basis of the decision we made was to preserve the integrity of the trial.&nbsp;&nbsp;@Dunford, Kit&nbsp;I’d appreciate some support for the first day, if your team are able to provide it tomorrow. The hearing will start at 10:30 at the royal courts of justice.&nbsp;&nbsp;Many thanks&nbsp;A&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From: Priscilla Mendes &lt;pmendes@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Friday, October 3, 2025 12:17:41 PMTo: Dunford, Kit &lt;Kit.Dunford@fticonsulting.com&gt;; Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Dougie Inglis &lt;dInglis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Strat Comm Pogust Goodhead &lt;pogustgoodhead@fticonsulting.com&gt;Subject: Re: Comms prep - NOx PTR &nbsp;Hi Kit,&nbsp;For the PTR, we already have a case memo for journalists awaiting Legal’s sign-off. We’ve also compiled a list of reporters following the claim, to whom we’ll circulate the PTR outcome - including the trial timeline, which has been one of the most frequent media enquiries.&nbsp;On PG’s potential step-back, I am awaiting updates from Legal/Board. Another pending issue is on what can be disclosed regarding Peter Gallhenger’s and the Emissions team situation - as it might be raised by journos too.&nbsp;In any case,&nbsp;@Anna Varga&nbsp;has kindly agreed to meet with the comms team next week to discuss the PR strategy going forward.&nbsp;Best,Pri&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Priscilla&nbsp;MendesChief&nbsp;External&nbsp;Affairs&nbsp;and&nbsp;Strategy&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;717From: Dunford, Kit &lt;Kit.Dunford@fticonsulting.com&gt;Sent: Friday, October 3, 2025 11:31 amTo: Paula Razera &lt;prazera@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Priscilla Mendes &lt;pmendes@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dougie Inglis &lt;dInglis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Strat Comm Pogust Goodhead &lt;pogustgoodhead@fticonsulting.com&gt;Subject: Comms prep - NOx PTR &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;&nbsp;Dear Pri, Paula,&nbsp;Good to see there’s no coverage from The Lawyer at this stage.&nbsp;I wanted to check in regarding your plans for the NOx PTR on Monday, and whether you’ve prepared any reactive communications given the likely press interest around PG potentially stepping back as co-lead on a temporary basis. Additionally, are either of you planning to attend in person?&nbsp;Please let me know if we can support on this.&nbsp;Many thanks,Kit&nbsp;Kit DunfordManaging Director, Strategic Communications&nbsp;FTI Consulting+44 (0)7717 417 038 kit.dunford@fticonsulting.com&nbsp;200 Aldersgate | Aldersgate StreetLondon | EC1A 4HD | United Kingdomwww.fticonsulting.com&nbsp;&nbsp;Confidentiality Notice: This email and any attachments may be confidential and protected by legal privilege. If you are not the intended recipient, be aware that any disclosure, copying, distribution or use of the e-mail or any attachment is prohibited. If you have received this email in error, please notify us immediately by replying to the sender and then delete this copy and the reply from your system. Thank you for your cooperation. FTI Consulting LLP. Registered Number OC372614. Registered in England and Wales at 200 Aldersgate, Aldersgate Street, London, EC1A 4HD. A full list of Members is available for inspection at the registered address. "}

