Draft:
&nbsp;
(The Side Letter is to be privileged and confidential (as is the Pan NOx AA)).

&nbsp;
1. Terms and phrases defined in the Pan NOx Agency Agreement (“Pan NOx AA”) shall have the same meaning in the Side Letter, unless otherwise defined herein.&nbsp;

&nbsp;
2. The following terms and phrases shall have the following meanings:
&nbsp;
“GLOs” means the group litigation orders of the Court in respect of the Lead Cases, listed on Annex A.
&nbsp;
“Lead Cases” shall mean, collectively, the following cases referred to in the Pan NOx AA in the definitions of Lead Group Litigation and Additional Lead
 Group Litigation as “The Mercedes-Benz NOx Emissions Group Litigation”, the “Ford Litigation”, the “Nissan/Renault Litigation” and the “Peugeot Citroën Litigation”.
&nbsp;
“PG Common Work “ means, collectively,&nbsp; the Common Work being done currently, or to be done, by PG as a current Lead Solicitor for the purposes of the
 Pan NOx AA and GLOs, as such work is described in general terms on Annex B as that may be updated from time to time by agreement between Leigh Day and PG with each acting reasonably and&nbsp; in good faith to achieve success in the trials or by settlement within
 the Litigation), and all work reasonably incidental and/or related to any of the foregoing.
&nbsp;
“PG Personnel” means, collectively, the PG personnel, carrying out the PG Common Work,&nbsp; listed on Annex C, as that may be updated, from time to time, for
 any additions or removals by notification by PG to Leigh Day and with respect to any addition (a) following consultation by PG with Leigh Day regarding the same and (b) subject to any objection thereto by Leigh Day, acting reasonably and in good faith, on
 the basis solely that such addition would give rise to a conflict (i) of interest with respect to the conduct of the litigation of any of the Leading Cases or (ii) with any of the terms of the GLOs).

&nbsp;
“Step-Down Date” means the date on which the Court issues an order approving PG’s resignation as a Lead Solicitor in each of the Lead Cases.
&nbsp;
3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Leigh Day irrevocably acknowledges to, and agrees with, PG that:
&nbsp;
(a) Leigh Day will not approve or support the addition of any other Lead Solicitor (in addition to Leigh Day) for the purposes of the Pan NOx AA and/or
 any of the GLOs, other than PG, so that Leigh Day remains the sole Leading Solicitor in the Lead Cases whilst PG is not a Leading Solicitor therein;
&nbsp;
(b)&nbsp; with effect from the Step-Down Date Leigh Day shall be deemed to have:
&nbsp;
(i) determined that the PG Team are suitably skilled solicitors with the relevant expertise for the purposes of Clause 8 of the Pan
 NOx AA and each of the GLOs;
&nbsp;
(ii) authorised the PG Team to carry out, and delegated to the PG Team the carrying out of, the PG Common Work; and
&nbsp;
(iii) acknowledged, and agreed with PG, that in respect of matters concerning the PG Team (including, without limitation, the PG Common Work) PG shall
 continue to supervise the PG Team and give directions and instructions to the PG Team, and Leigh Day shall have the right to supervise such matters as requisite and consistent with its role as Lead Solicitor delegating PG Common Work to PG;
&nbsp;
(c) the charges for the reasonable time spent by the PG Team in carrying out the PG Common Work shall form part of the Basic Charges and will be charged
 at the hourly rates set out in SCHEDULE 2 of the Pan-Nox AA as if it had been performed by PG as a Lead Solicitor;

&nbsp;
(d)&nbsp; any disbursements incurred by the PG Team on PG Common Work shall be Disbursements for the purposes of the Pan NOx AA; and
&nbsp;
(e) Leigh Day shall support PG’s re-appointment as a Lead Solicitor in the Lead Cases (both in the steering committee for the Lead Group Litigation and
 in the relevant applications to the Court for the Leading Cases) when PG notifies Leigh Day that it seeks such re-appointment on the basis that, acting reasonably and in good faith, PG has determined that such re-appointment would not be a distraction to the
 conduct of litigation of the Leading Cases in the best interests of the claimants.; and
