Thanks Matt, Alessia.&nbsp;Please see attached the 24 Sept letter referred to in the Renault notice Alessia asked for. &nbsp;Additionally, noting that the Renault application asked for confirmation by 4pm of whether we could provide the request information, we have prepared the short draft email below. If we’re not able to get the broader letter to the Defendants out in the next hour, we’d propose sending this by way of interim response. Do let us know if you have any thoughts. &nbsp;Jess &nbsp;***********************************&nbsp;Dear Sirs/Madams, &nbsp;We acknowledge receipt of Renault’s request for information regarding the individual within Pogust Goodhead has assumed overall responsibility for the Emissions litigation.&nbsp;We confirm that we propose to share an update with the Defendant firms addressing this point in advance of the stated deadline of noon on 25 September 2025. &nbsp;On this basis, we confirm that there is no need for Renault to issue the application notice. &nbsp;&nbsp;Yours faithfully &nbsp;Pogust Goodhead&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateFrom: Matthew Getz &lt;Matthew.Getz@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 14:45To: Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Turvey &lt;Nick.Turvey@pallasllp.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Craig Shuttleworth &lt;cshuttleworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;Subject: RE: Draft email to Ds on stepping down&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thanks Jessica. It sounds very positive.&nbsp;Would you like us to write up the detailed heads of terms?&nbsp;When we get back your comments on the witness statement, we will update it to take account of these developments (just the progress to agreement, not the details).&nbsp;We