down and see what the response is. Said to keep it under review. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Costs Martyn agreed that there “wasn’t the slightest chance” of LD agreeing common costs without PG’s agreement. Stated that PG and LD were in a joint enterprise.On costs protection – we sought confirmation from LD on the wording in the agency agreement “protection against liability for common work”. Martyn stated that once PG are no longer Lead Sols they would not anticipate coming to PG for approval, but would involve everyone in the discussion. We said that given the broader SteerCo context, we could let go of “express approval”&nbsp;Relationship between PG &amp; LD Martyn stated that LD is “desperately in need” of the PG team and would want the PG team working on the case as normal. Stated that once this is resolved he would totally support PG coming back in. PG welcomed and echoed these sentiments. &nbsp;Next steps We stated that the letter to the Defendants would be sent ASAP, and that the application would follow hopefully today / possibly tomorrow. Lizzy (Slater &amp; Gordon) suggested that they could share a headline agreement for PG to see before formally stepping down (in advance of a more detailed agreement next week)A call was proposed for Monday or Tuesday next week to discuss nuts and bolts of how PG’s step down / ongoing work with LD would work in practice. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Jessica&nbsp;FechnerAssociateThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Please note that our general terms and conditions apply to all our services. These general terms and conditions include a clause stipulating that our liability is excluded for damage