lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Melissa Ferrari &lt;mferrari@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Ainsworth &lt;tainsworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: G3 reservations&nbsp;Dear All,&nbsp;We wanted to share an update from Gramercy following Joe’s approach relating to the specific clauses discussed during our very long session with Richard Coleman KC on Friday.&nbsp;On a strictly confidential basis and in the spirit of transparency, we wanted to share with you their response received early this morning.&nbsp;Whilst I’ve not shared yet another version of this lengthy agreement to save everyone’s time, I’m happy for @Helena&nbsp;to provide you with sections of the regulatory points as described by Marc Zelina in his email.&nbsp;Going forward, we will ensure that any contact with any of our funders is managed carefully with a clear process stipulated for any request for information. Should you be approached on any matters, please feel free to refer to @Carolina&nbsp;in the first instance.&nbsp;Many thanksA&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaInterim&nbsp;Chief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From:&nbsp;Marc Zelina &lt;mzelina@gramercy.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;08 September 2025 01:43To:&nbsp;Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nick Paolazzi &lt;npaolazzi@gramercy.com&gt;; James Taylor &lt;JTaylor@gramercy.com&gt;; Joshua Katz &lt;jkatz@gramercy.com&gt;; Thomas Norgaard &lt;tnorgaard@gramercy.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: G3 Facility Clauses&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Joe,&nbsp;Thank you for sending this email and bringing this matter to our attention. It is very unfortunate that Tom Goodhead kept the firm leadership in the dark about the G3 facility. As Alicia and others know, we spent considerable time discussing the G3 credit facility with Tom and made every effort to close it prior to the end of June.&nbsp;As you may know, certain provisions within the G3 credit agreement were flagged by Tom in June as “regulatory points”. These provisions were subsequently negotiated directly between our regulatory counsel, Juliet Oliver from Kingsley Napley (who just recently left her position as Deputy Chief Executive and General Counsel at the SRA for over a decade), and PG’s regulatory counsel, Weightmans. After several weeks of negotiations, both PG and Gramercy agreed on the precise language for all of these “regulatory points”. In fact, on Tuesday, July 29, PG’s transaction counsel, McDermott, sent the attached light redline of the Credit Agreement (which does not have any changes to the “regulatory points”) to our counsel and Tom let us know that he was prepared to sign the attached July 29 draft Credit Agreement and close the facility as soon as possible. Unfortunately, Tom did not provide an operating budget for the use of proceeds under the G3 facility. This was the last open item for Gramercy to obtain our necessary approvals to close and we had been seeking the budget from PG for several months. Nick and Josh even went to London during the week of July 21 to meet with Tom personally to discuss the G3 operating budget but he did not agree to meet them in person. Instead, he dialed in by Zoom for a short time from the Netherlands and left the budget unresolved.&nbsp;As a result of the careful process and advice that both PG and Gramercy received from highly capable regulatory lawyers, Gramercy is comfortable that the G3 credit facility does not violate any applicable laws or disciplinary rules or place PG attorneys at risk. Notwithstanding the foregoing, Gramercy takes the concerns of the PG attorneys very seriously and would like to help build goodwill. Accordingly, Gramercy is willing to agree to the following with respect to the provisions that you cite below:&nbsp;Section 4.51 – Gramercy is prepared to waive our rights regarding the obligation for PG to appoint a Key Person to the board of each Stichting. Accordingly, PG is free to appoint directors in accordance with the internal governing documents of the Stichtings.&nbsp;Section 5.12 – Gramercy is prepared to accept PG’s proposal and has no desire to be allowed inside a Confidentiality Ring.&nbsp;Section 5.15 – Gramercy believes that the access to the case management system is already subject to Disciplinary Rules but please clarify if you believe differently.&nbsp;Section 5.43 – Gramercy is prepared to work together with PG to find alternative arrangements.&nbsp;Section 5.49 – Gramercy is prepared to waive our rights regarding the representation. Accordingly, PG is not in any way constrained or obligated based on this representation.&nbsp;Section 6.17 – Gramercy is prepared to accept PG’s proposal and make clear that regulatory obligations trump any such consents.&nbsp;Section 8.22 and 8.24 – As you know, these provisions address a handful of obligations in the Credit Agreement. Gramercy is prepared to agree that all PG obligations under 5.12(b), 5.49(a), 5.49(b) and 5.49(d) are subject to PG’s determination on what it considers to be its own regulatory obligations even if it conflicts with the Qualified Independent Legal Ethics Counsel.&nbsp;Finally, we are willing to ask our regulatory counsel, Juliet Oliver, to make herself available for any further questions that you or PG’s lawyers have with respect to the G3 credit agreement.&nbsp;Please do let us know if you have any questions. Regards,Marc&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;07 September 2025 17:50To:&nbsp;Céline Gisele Beryl Barnwell &lt;cbarnwell@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alison Webb &lt;awebb@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Faranak Ghajavand &lt;fghajavand@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Felipe Hotta &lt;fhotta@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Guy Robson &lt;grobson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Georgina Fallows &lt;gfallows@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Melissa Ferrari &lt;mferrari@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Ainsworth &lt;tainsworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: G3 reservations&nbsp;Team -&nbsp;Following up on the below. Per Friday’s debrief, Leading Counsel was clear that the G3 credit facility does not place any of us at risk of breaching our professional obligations. That said, you have raised legitimate points about how several provisions could impact your case strategies and day-to-day activities. While we must respect the rights of our creditors, we do not want to expend undue resources on processes that divert from our primary duty of servicing our cases and our clients.&nbsp;To that end, Gramercy has agreed to revisit these terms in a manner indicative of good faith and renewed confidence in the firm. The Board will continue to seek your input as this process promptly proceeds (and welcomes volunteers to collaborate on this effort). In the meanwhile, if you have continued questions or concerns do not hesitate to contact me.&nbsp;Thank you again for being upfront with your views on this. I look forward to working together on these matters as we implement more formalized protocols under our new business model of transparency and teamwork.&nbsp;Best,Joe&nbsp;​​​​Joseph&nbsp;MorenoDirectorFrom: Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Friday, September 5, 2025 at 14:00To: Céline Gisele Beryl Barnwell &lt;cbarnwell@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Alison Webb &lt;awebb@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Faranak Ghajavand &lt;fghajavand@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Felipe Hotta &lt;fhotta@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Guy Robson &lt;grobson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Georgina Fallows &lt;gfallows@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Leila-Zoe Mezoughi &lt;lzmezoughi@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Melissa Ferrari &lt;mferrari@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Tom Ainsworth &lt;tainsworth@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;,"}

