Hi Nick &nbsp;We have received some further queries from our brokers regarding the proposed topup to the Nox policies (+£17m LOI)&nbsp;They want a call tomorrow to discuss 1b, would it be possible to discuss with you on a quick call before hand?&nbsp;Query from insurer below, let me know if you are available &nbsp;TomOn the economics - we will review the existing cross-collateralisation arrangements with a view to how they might be adapted for our purposes. We do have two requests on this side of things though:We note that for the existing arrangements, PG is the only claimant-side party. Our current view is that we would also want Gramercy as a party, either in its own right or as a guarantor. Is this acceptable to PG/Gramercy?On a related point, we would like to better understand how any settlement proceeds would flow through the existing waterfall(s), including the arrangements with cash flow up to Gramercy. Essentially, we would like to be able to understand what the effect of, for example, a settlement with Mercedes, would have on the money flowing through the waterfall in order to assess the extent to which such a settlement would then protect us from adverse results against other defendants. It would also be useful to be able to see the effect of varying levels of settlement. We assume that PG has excel models which would allow us to understand this - could we see copies?&nbsp;&nbsp;From: James Burke &lt;James.Burke2@wtwco.com&gt; Sent: 06 November 2025 11:09To: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation - Toremis&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Thanks Tom.&nbsp;I’ve been in touch with Toremis by email this morning and they have sent the following update. Would you be able to assist with their request please:I think we have all we need from you/PG on the merits now. We just need to reflect internally on the overall position - this shouldn't take us too long.On the economics - we will review the existing cross-collateralisation arrangements with a view to how they might be adapted for our purposes. We do have two requests on this side of things though:We note that for the existing arrangements, PG is the only claimant-side party. Our current view is that we would also want Gramercy as a party, either in its own right or as a guarantor. Is this acceptable to PG/Gramercy?On a related point, we would like to better understand how any settlement proceeds would flow through the existing waterfall(s), including the arrangements with cash flow up to Gramercy. Essentially, we would like to be able to understand what the effect of, for example, a settlement with Mercedes, would have on the money flowing through the waterfall in order to assess the extent to which such a settlement would then protect us from adverse results against other defendants. It would also be useful to be able to see the effect of varying levels of settlement. We assume that PG has excel models which would allow us to understand this - could we see copies?Let me know if you need to discuss. I will be available this afternoon.Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global &nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116) On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated