ronouns are: he / him​&nbsp;Follow&nbsp;us&nbsp;on&nbsp;twitter&nbsp;@clydecoemp​​​​&nbsp;From: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 17 October 2025 17:29To: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;; Matthew Getz &lt;matthew.getz@pallasllp.com&gt;; James Newton &lt;james.newton@pallasllp.com&gt;; Urquhart, Charles &lt;charles.urquhart@clydeco.com&gt;; Riceman, Sarah &lt;sarah.riceman@clydeco.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: FW: Notice of Resignation&nbsp;See below – a distinct change in tone!&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Friday, 17 October 2025 at 17:27To: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Notice of ResignationHi Raminder,&nbsp;Thanks for coming back to me on this.&nbsp;&nbsp;I intend on responding to your email in full, however I am due to be in court on Monday, so I will not be able to comply with the requested deadline of 5pm on Monday 20 October 2025. I will respond as soon as I am able to.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks again, and I hope you have a nice weekend. I hope Alicia is feeling better as well as I believe she is unwell.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Friday, October 17, 2025 3:00 PMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Notice of Resignation &nbsp;Dear Michael,&nbsp;Thank you for your email.&nbsp; I have also been provided with your emails to Alicia from today regarding a potential article in The Times, suggestions of criminal conduct and concerns over Gramercy.&nbsp; This email responds to them&nbsp;together.&nbsp;As previously communicated to you, we will not be releasing you from your notice period.&nbsp; Your continued attempts to leave earlier than your contract allows are proving disruptive to our efforts to safeguard good governance within the firm.&nbsp;&nbsp;In addition, your conduct threatens to seriously damage morale and be more disruptive than helpful, taking account of the best interests of our clients.&nbsp;We are, therefore, minded to&nbsp;give you the option of being placed&nbsp;on&nbsp;paid leave for the remainder of your notice period.&nbsp; We would view that as regrettable since we are in the midst of the PDD Trial and would much prefer to have you remain&nbsp;working&nbsp;on the team.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We therefore give you the choice of either to (i) stay working throughout the remainder of your notice period or (ii) go on&nbsp;paid&nbsp;leave effective immediately.&nbsp;If you continue to try to exit early,&nbsp;given the unparticularised nature of your allegations, we can only conclude that you are grasping for reasons to engineer such an exit for your own reasons, which is unprofessional, threatens breaches of your employment contract, and is not in the best interests of our clients.&nbsp; We put you on notice that we will not hesitate to take legal action against you to enforce your employment contract (in particular your notice period and all covenants), nor will we hesitate to take action against any firm that might seek to employ you ahead of your notice period expiring or in breach of your covenants.&nbsp;If you choose to remain&nbsp;working&nbsp;at the firm, we must insist that you focus solely on your work and only raise any further concerns with sufficient particularity and justification so that we can understand them fully and investigate them if necessary.&nbsp; Unclear and unparticularised allegations as you have been raising for the past several weeks are simply improper and must stop.&nbsp;Regarding the specific points raised in your emails:&nbsp;We are looking into your concerns over Gramercy’s recent input into the Litigation Management Agreement and Agency Agreements. &nbsp;Your email was lengthy, so we need time to fully digest your concerns, but we intend to respond early next week.&nbsp; For the avoidance of doubt, the remainder of this email was prepared before we received your email regarding Gramercy.Your suggestion that you cannot act in the best interests of our clients under supervision from other staff is not understood.&nbsp; If you continue to believe this is the case, please explain which members of staff and why, by precise reference to specific provisions of your contract or the SRA Code of Conduct, say this is so.You refer vaguely to potential criminal conduct.&nbsp; This is obviously a very serious allegation.&nbsp; Please now state clearly and unequivocally what precise conduct you are referring to and by which specific people so that we can investigate immediately.As you are aware, the firm has already taken robust action against Tom Goodhead.&nbsp; We take our obligations to our stakeholders extremely seriously and there is not, therefore, any basis for you to seek to exit early.&nbsp; Even if there has been improper behaviour at the Firm – and rest assured, we will investigate any such allegations seriously – that does not give you any justification, under either your contract or your regulatory obligations. Conjecture about what may or may not be published in The Times&nbsp;does not change that position.I look forward to hearing back from you regarding whether you wish to continue working on the case&nbsp;at PG&nbsp;or go onto&nbsp;paid&nbsp;leave by return and in any event by 5pm on Monday 20 October 2025. We remain hopeful that you will agree to continue to work&nbsp;at PG&nbsp;throughout the PDD Trial.&nbsp;In the meantime, and given your reference to protected disclosures and your suggestion that you will cease working on Monday despite the terms of your contract, please confirm that you have and will continue to preserve all documents that might be relevant to your employment with PG and associated covenants.&nbsp;All of the firm’s rights are fully reserved.&nbsp;Kind regards,Raminder&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Friday, 17 October 2025 at 09:34To: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;, Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Notice of ResignationHi Raminder,&nbsp;Just following up on the below.&nbsp;We have now reached the 17 October - my requested leave date (having already requested to be released prior to this date).&nbsp;Since my last email, further material developments have occurred meaning I must insist I am permitted to leave as soon as possible. Not only do these developments give me immediate concerns regarding Gramercy's continued direct involvement in the managing and supervision of the NOx Litigation, these developments also are intentionally preventing me in acting in what I believe to be in my clients best interests. Furthermore, they also risk causing significant damage to my professional reputation:&nbsp;email chains which confirm Gramercy, as recently as September, were directly involved in the NOX Litigation and they have been giving direct input into Litigations Management Agreements and Agency Agreements. Yesterday, Anna Varga instructed a member of staff to engage with the company retained by Gramercy to give direct input into these documents - despite assurances given to me and the staff directly by the Board and Anna that Gramercy are not involved in the Litigation;I am unable to continue to fulfil the role of acting in my clients best interests under the instruction of other members of staff;the prospect of criminal proceedings being levied against staff within the firm who are now involved in the NOx Litigation; andthe impending release of a Times article regarding 'misuse of litigation funds, a generally toxic culture, and allowing bullying sexism and sexual harassment with specific instances of senior male staff.'&nbsp;I am afraid I am unable to continue to act in my role at Pogust Goodhead. Please confirm by return that I will be permitted to leave my role effective immediately. I am due to travel to London on Sunday night which I will do to empty the flat and I will then attend the office on Monday to return my laptop.&nbsp;&nbsp;I look forward to hearing from you. All of my rights are reserved.&nbsp;&nbsp;Regards,&nbsp;Michael​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;29 September 2025 10:04 AMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Notice of Resignation&nbsp;Hi Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;Thank you for your note. I’ll review the content today and come back to you soon as I can with a response.&nbsp;&nbsp;In the meantime, please do not take any action with regards to flights or any other matters outlined in your email, without seeking further approval. Thank you.&nbsp;&nbsp;Regards&nbsp;Raminder&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Monday, September 29, 2025 9:53:23 AMTo:&nbsp;Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Notice of Resignation&nbsp;Dear Raminder,Thank you&nbsp;for coming back to me and for accepting my resignation. My apologies for the delay in coming back to you, as I’m sure you are aware there are a lot of things in the air!Noting your comments regarding my resignation being premature, I disagree with that assessment, but we are where we are. What is important is that we find a way to move forward that ensures the clients of Pogust Goodhead (and other firms) are not prejudiced or detrimentally impacted moving forward and that we are all content with. I trust that my conduct since submitting my notice demonstrates that I am committed to working with the firm to progress this in a professional and orderly fashion. This email has some detail in it so if it is easier for us to hop on a call to try and cut through bits of it or to have a quicker conversation, I'm more than happy to do so.&nbsp;This email is in two parts: i) to address my notice period and when may be a good time for me to depart the firm; and ii) to address on-going travel and litigation needs with a view to finding a pragmatic way to handle future travel etc.Notice PeriodI agree that we need to work collaboratively to find an appropriate point for me to leave the firm, both to ensure the clients are protected and not disadvantaged, and to ensure that I am protected and not prejudiced. My current leave date is I understand the 15 December 2025. There are"}

