 protected with Michael’s DOB – 24121988).&nbsp;I have saved a copy to file.&nbsp;Please let me know if I can log this on HiBob and if you need me to do anything else.&nbsp;Best,C &nbsp;​​​​HR&nbsp;TeamHR&nbsp;TeamFrom: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 01 December 2025 08:45To: HR Team &lt;hr@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: M Burke&nbsp;Dear colleagues,&nbsp;Please find attached a Statement of Fitness for Work, which verifies that I have not been, and remain not fit for work for the period of 20 November to 15 December 2025. Please note this is password protected (as was provided by my GP) and the password is my date of birth in the following format: DDMMYYYY.&nbsp;&nbsp;I have tried to avoid using this sick note, since it was provided on 20 November by taking holiday, in an attempt to reconcile me being able to return to work, but unfortunately, this has not been possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;Under clause 13.4 of my contract of employment, I am entitled to received up to 10 days company sick pay. The days, commencing from 1 December 2025 run through until 12 December 2025 (inc) fall within this entitlement and should be paid in full. I will endeavour of course to make myself available to return to work prior to 15 December 2025, mindful that I am still contributing to my team, and my clients. I am also mindful of the firm's ask for me to provide a thorough handover. I will endeavour to provide a handover on those matters which I have conduct of as best I can before I depart the firm (Pan-NOx, Ford, Volvo, British Airways, UEFA and easyJet) and will be in the office on 15 December to hold any meetings required.&nbsp;I will also keep myself abreast of any developments on the litigations such that I am fully versed in any material changes in the event I am able to return to work prior to the 15 December 2025.&nbsp;&nbsp;I note that I presently have 6 days remaining of my holiday entitlement for the year. I would be grateful if this accrued holiday is paid to me in my final salary and that this is confirmed by return.&nbsp;&nbsp;As above, if I am able to return to work prior to the 15 December 2025, then I will certainly endeavour to. I am very mindful of my commitments to my team, and to my clients. In the event I am not fit to return to work before 15 December 2025, I will be present in the office on 15 December 2025 to complete my last working day, bid my colleagues farewell, and handover my equipment.&nbsp;Please confirm this by return.&nbsp;&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;"}
